    "One of the most catastrophic financial traps awaiting young people in their twenties is the Credential Treadmill. For generations, society has taught that the only legitimate path to financial security is acquiring university degrees, prestigious diplomas, and corporate certifications. Young adults are encouraged to take on fifty thousand, one hundred thousand, or even two hundred thousand dollars of non-dischargeable student loan debt to obtain credentials in subjects that have virtually zero direct commercial application.",
