    "The economic mathematics of this path are disastrous. A young person who graduates at twenty-two with eighty thousand dollars of student loan debt begins their adult life with a massive negative net worth. Before they can save a dollar, invest in an asset, or build a business, they must dedicate hundreds of dollars each month to servicing interest payments on an asset that depreciates in relative value every year.",
    "Student loan debt acts as a financial ball and chain that restricts your life choices. When you carry heavy debt burdens, you cannot afford to take calculated career risks. You cannot accept a commission-only sales role that could teach you high-income skills, you cannot work as an apprentice to a wealthy founder for low pay, and you cannot launch a startup with three months of runway.",
